-- החלטת ועדת המעקב העליונה — פרקי זמן השהייה הנדרשים לצורך קידום לדרגה 2
-- עד 6 (19.2.2015): the supreme follow-up committee, under §160 of the base
-- agreement of 25.12.2008, lengthens by a month every waiting period of
-- §38(ב) and §38(ו) and the longest a qualified teacher may be held back
-- under §38(ט), from 1.3.2015; keeps the decision of 19.9.2010 for one who
-- leaves the service and whom the extra month alone would have kept out of
-- it; and approves, once, 1,800 promotions to grades 7–9 in תשע"ד and
-- תשע"ה beyond §38(ז)'s quotas, filled in three rounds (1.9.2014, 1.8.2015,
-- 1.9.2015).
--
-- An amendment encodes what it changes, dated: the new periods are written
-- here as months, from 1.3.2015, beside §38's years, which this file
-- imports and never re-encodes; the 2010 decision is imported where §ד
-- applies it. The Ministry's letter of 25.12.2008 on professional
-- development hours, and the evaluation measures of תשע"ב and תשע"ה, are
-- not in the corpus: what they say of a teacher is an input.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT parties
IMPORT `base-agreement-38`
IMPORT `base-agreement-160`
IMPORT `2010-09-19_ofek-hadash_vaadat-maakav_darga-promotion-at-service-end`

-- The day the new periods start (§§א–ג).
`1 March 2015` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2015

-- Months in a number of years.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `years as months` y IS
    y TIMES 12

DECLARE `stay-periods decision action` IS ONE OF
    `approve promotions to grades 7–9 beyond §38(ז) in תשע"ד and תשע"ה`

§ `החלטת ועדת המעקב העליונה — פרקי זמן השהייה ומכסת 1,800 המשרות — 19.2.2015`

-- akn:preamble The decision's frame: a label row with no text of its own.

-- The title, with the handwritten date of the decision.
@ref akn:preamble/p1
`the day of the stay-periods decision` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 19 2 2015

-- akn:preamble/p2 The Registrar's stamp: registered on 21.06.2015 as no. 74/2015; no rule of the decision.

-- The opening: the committee decides under §160 of the base agreement
-- ("הסכם אופק חדש"), on promotion in grades of reform teachers — §38(ז)
-- among them — because teachers were placed in grades 7 and 8 up to תשע"ד
-- beyond §38(ז)'s rates. The three who sign it (the wages commissioner,
-- the union's secretary-general and the Ministry's director-general) are
-- the three §160 seats.
@ref akn:preamble/p3 akn:conclusions/p1 akn:conclusions/t1 akn:conclusions/p2
`the stay-periods decision's signatories` MEANS
    LIST `the wages commissioner at the Treasury`, `the teachers' union`, `the Ministry of Education`

#ASSERT all (GIVEN p YIELD elem p `the supreme committee's members`) `the stay-periods decision's signatories`

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off: a label row with no text of its own.

§§ `א. פרקי זמן השהייה לדרגות 2 עד 6 — במקום סעיף 38(ב)`

-- From 1.3.2015 §38(ב) reads: from grade 1 to 2 and from 2 to 3, two years
-- and a month in the grade below; from 3 to 4, 4 to 5 and 5 to 6, three
-- years and a month. Written as months: 25 and 37.
@ref akn:art_a
GIVEN `to grade` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `months in the grade below for promotion to, as the 2015 decision sets them` `to grade` IS
    (`years as months` (`years in the grade below for promotion to` `to grade`)) PLUS 1

#ASSERT map `months in the grade below for promotion to, as the 2015 decision sets them` (LIST 2, 3, 4, 5, 6) EQUALS LIST 25, 25, 37, 37, 37

§§ `ב. פרקי זמן השהייה לדרגות 7 עד 9 — במקום סעיף 38(ו)`

-- From 1.3.2015 §38(ו) reads: from grade 6 to 7, 7 to 8 and 8 to 9, three
-- years and a month — the same rule as §א, from §38's three years.
@ref akn:art_b
#ASSERT map `months in the grade below for promotion to, as the 2015 decision sets them` (LIST 7, 8, 9) EQUALS LIST 37, 37, 37

§§ `ג. עיכוב הקידום לדרגות 7 עד 9 — במקום סעיף 38(ט)`

-- From 1.3.2015 §38(ט) reads: notwithstanding (ח), one who met (ה)'s
-- conditions for grades 7–9 is not held back more than 3 years and a
-- month from grade 7, 4 years and a month from 8, 5 years and a month from
-- 9, subject to a free place in the quota.
@ref akn:art_c
GIVEN `to grade` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `months a qualified teacher may be held back from, as the 2015 decision sets them` `to grade` IS
    (`years as months` (`years a qualified teacher may be held back from` `to grade`)) PLUS 1

#ASSERT map `months a qualified teacher may be held back from, as the 2015 decision sets them` (LIST 7, 8, 9) EQUALS LIST 37, 49, 61

GIVEN d IS A DATE, `to grade` IS A NUMBER, `months held back` IS A NUMBER, `free places` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `goes before the scores on` d `to grade` `months held back` `free places` IF
    IF d `is on or after` `1 March 2015`
    THEN     `months held back` AT LEAST `months a qualified teacher may be held back from, as the 2015 decision sets them` `to grade`
         AND `free places` GREATER THAN 0
    ELSE `goes before the scores` `to grade` (`months held back` DIVIDED BY 12) `free places`

#ASSERT NOT `goes before the scores on` `1 March 2015` 7 36 5
#ASSERT `goes before the scores on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2015) 7 36 5
#ASSERT NOT `goes before the scores on` `1 March 2015` 7 37 0

§§ `ד. מי שעומד לסיים את העסקתו — החלטת 2010`

-- One who meets §1(א), (ב) and (ד) of the decision of 19.9.2010 ("החלטת
-- 2010") and would meet §1(ג) — his waiting period ending on the day he
-- leaves — but for this decision's extra month, is promoted as if the
-- waiting period ended on the 31 July before he leaves; §2 of that
-- decision (the promotion from 1 August) applies to him too. So the 2010
-- decision is applied with (ג) tested against the waiting period as it ran
-- before this decision: `employee at the end of service`'s waiting period
-- here is the one §38's years give.
@ref akn:art_d
GIVEN e IS AN `employee at the end of service`
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the day the waiting period is taken to end, by the 2015 decision's §ד` e IS
    `the day the waiting period is taken to end` e

GIVEN e IS AN `employee at the end of service`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `the promotion of §ד starts on` e IS
    `the promotion of §1 starts on` e

-- A teacher in grade 5 who leaves on 31.8.2015, whose three years in it
-- under §38 end that day (the decision's 37 months would end on 30.9.2015),
-- is promoted from 1.8.2015.
`a teacher leaving on 31.8.2015` MEANS
    `employee at the end of service` WITH
        `employed on Ofek Hadash terms`             IS TRUE
        `ends employment in the civil service on`   IS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2015
        `the waiting period for the next grade ends on` IS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2015
        `met the other conditions for promotion on 31 July before the end` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the day the waiting period is taken to end, by the 2015 decision's §ד` `a teacher leaving on 31.8.2015` EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 7 2015
#ASSERT `the promotion of §ד starts on` `a teacher leaving on 31.8.2015` EQUALS JUST (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2015)

§§ `ה. מי שהיה זכאי לקידום מ־1.3.2015`

-- §§א–ב dated: from 1.3.2015 the decision's months, before it §38's years.
-- §ה: they reach every promotion due from 1.3.2015 on, whenever the
-- waiting period began — the test is the day of the promotion.
@ref akn:art_e
GIVEN `promotion day` IS A DATE, `to grade` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `months in the grade below for promotion to on` `promotion day` `to grade` IS
    IF `promotion day` `is on or after` `1 March 2015`
    THEN `months in the grade below for promotion to, as the 2015 decision sets them` `to grade`
    ELSE `years as months` (`years in the grade below for promotion to` `to grade`)

#ASSERT `months in the grade below for promotion to on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2015) 7 EQUALS 36
#ASSERT `months in the grade below for promotion to on` `1 March 2015` 7 EQUALS 37

-- A teacher whose 24 months in grade 1 ended on 1.3.2015 waits a month
-- more; one who began grade 1 before 1.3.2013 is no exception.
GIVEN `months in the grade` IS A NUMBER, `promotion day` IS A DATE, `to grade` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has waited long enough for promotion on` `months in the grade` `promotion day` `to grade` IF
    `months in the grade` AT LEAST `months in the grade below for promotion to on` `promotion day` `to grade`

#ASSERT NOT `has waited long enough for promotion on` 24 `1 March 2015` 2
#ASSERT `has waited long enough for promotion on` 24 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2015) 2


§§ `ו. מכסת המשרות — 1,800`

-- Notwithstanding §38(ז), promotion to grades 7–9 is approved once, in
-- תשע"ד and תשע"ה, for 1,800 positions ("מכסת המשרות"): beyond the quotas
-- of 10%, 5% and 3%, which this does not reach (F-ofek-hadash-maakav-2015-a).
@ref akn:art_f
`the quota of positions` MEANS 1800

-- The two school years, by the calendar year each opens in (convention
-- dates.school-year): תשע"ד in 2013 and תשע"ה in 2014.
@ref akn:art_f
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in the years of the quota of positions` d IF
        d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2013)
    AND d `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2015)

@ref akn:art_f
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `stay-periods decision action`
DECIDE `the one-time approval` IS
    PARTY `the State`
    MAY   `approve promotions to grades 7–9 beyond §38(ז) in תשע"ד and תשע"ה`

§§ `ז. מה אינו נכלל במכסת המשרות`

@desc A position in grades 7–9, as far as §ז asks whether it is one of the 1,800.
DECLARE `position in grades 7–9` HAS
    `held by a teacher placed in grades 7–9 at the signing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a free place for promotion to grade 9 at the signing`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- Teachers in grades 7–9 on the day the decision is signed, and the free
-- places for promotion to grade 9 on that day, are not in the 1,800.
@ref akn:art_g
GIVEN p IS A `position in grades 7–9`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `counts in the quota of positions` p IF
    NOT (p's `held by a teacher placed in grades 7–9 at the signing` OR p's `a free place for promotion to grade 9 at the signing`)

§§ `ח. סדר הקידום במסגרת מכסת המשרות`

@desc A teacher in the rounds of §ח, as far as its conditions ask.
DECLARE `candidate for the quota of positions` HAS
    `to grade`                                  IS A NUMBER @desc 7, 8 or 9 ("לפי העניין")
    `professional development hours completed on` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc the hours the Ministry's letter to the union of 25.12.2008 asks for the grade; not in the corpus
    `months in the grade below on 1.9.2014`       IS A NUMBER
    `months in the grade below on 1.8.2015`       IS A NUMBER
    `months in the grade below on 31.8.2015`      IS A NUMBER
    `evaluation of תשע"ב sufficient for the grade` IS A BOOLEAN @desc by the measures set for תשע"ב
    `retires on 31.8.2015`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `evaluation score of תשע"ה`                  IS A NUMBER

-- The professional development hours were completed by a day.
GIVEN c IS A `candidate for the quota of positions`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `completed the development hours by` c d IF
    CONSIDER c's `professional development hours completed on`
    WHEN JUST e THEN e `is on or before` d
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- The promotion is within the quota only, in the three rounds below.
@ref akn:art_h
`the rounds of the quota of positions` MEANS
    LIST DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2014, DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2015, DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2015

-- (1): promoted from 1.9.2014, one who by then (א) completed the
-- development hours, (ב) waited §38(ו)'s period — §38's own, the decision's
-- months starting only on 1.3.2015 (§ה) — and (ג) had a sufficient
-- תשע"ב evaluation.
@ref akn:art_h__para_1 akn:art_h__para_1__subpara_a akn:art_h__para_1__subpara_b akn:art_h__para_1__subpara_c
GIVEN c IS A `candidate for the quota of positions`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is in the first round` c IF
        `completed the development hours by` c (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2014)
    AND `has waited long enough for promotion on` (c's `months in the grade below on 1.9.2014`) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2014) (c's `to grade`)
    AND c's `evaluation of תשע"ב sufficient for the grade`

-- (2): if places are left after (1), promoted on 1.8.2015, one who (א)
-- completed the hours by 1.8.2015, (ב) waited the period by then, (ג) had
-- a sufficient תשע"ב evaluation and (ד) retires on 31.8.2015.
-- F-ofek-hadash-maakav-2015-b: (ב) names the period for grade 7 or 8 only;
-- the reading adopted is that a promotion to grade 9 asks its own period
-- too, as (1)(ב) does (convention reading.consistent). The period is the
-- decision's months, the promotion falling after 1.3.2015 (§ה).
@ref akn:art_h__para_2 akn:art_h__para_2__subpara_a akn:art_h__para_2__subpara_b akn:art_h__para_2__subpara_c akn:art_h__para_2__subpara_d
GIVEN c IS A `candidate for the quota of positions`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is in the second round` c IF
        `completed the development hours by` c (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2015)
    AND `has waited long enough for promotion on` (c's `months in the grade below on 1.8.2015`) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2015) (c's `to grade`)
    AND c's `evaluation of תשע"ב sufficient for the grade`
    AND c's `retires on 31.8.2015`

-- (3): if places are still left, promoted on 1.9.2015, one who (א)
-- completed the hours by 31.8.2015 and (ב) waited the period by then
-- (grade 9 as in (2)), and (ג) among them, the highest תשע"ה evaluations.
@ref akn:art_h__para_3 akn:art_h__para_3__subpara_a akn:art_h__para_3__subpara_b
GIVEN c IS A `candidate for the quota of positions`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be in the third round` c IF
        `completed the development hours by` c (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2015)
    AND `has waited long enough for promotion on` (c's `months in the grade below on 31.8.2015`) (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2015) (c's `to grade`)

GIVEN `places left` IS A NUMBER, cs IS A LIST OF `candidate for the quota of positions`
GIVETH A LIST OF `candidate for the quota of positions`
DECIDE `the first places by score` `places left` cs IS
    take `places left` (sortBy (GIVEN a, b YIELD a's `evaluation score of תשע"ה` AT LEAST b's `evaluation score of תשע"ה`) cs)

-- (3)(ג): the third round goes by the highest תשע"ה evaluations, as many
-- as there are places left.
@ref akn:art_h__para_3__subpara_c
GIVEN `places left` IS A NUMBER, cs IS A LIST OF `candidate for the quota of positions`
GIVETH A LIST OF `candidate for the quota of positions`
DECIDE `the third round` `places left` cs IS
    `the first places by score` `places left` (filter `may be in the third round` cs)

-- The three rounds over the 1,800. F-ofek-hadash-maakav-2015-c: rounds (1)
-- and (2) say who "will be promoted" and give no order when they hold more
-- teachers than the places left; the reading adopted orders them as round
-- (3) does, by the highest evaluation, the one order the decision gives
-- (convention reading.analogy).
GIVEN cs IS A LIST OF `candidate for the quota of positions`
GIVETH A LIST OF `candidate for the quota of positions`
DECIDE `promoted in the first round` cs IS
    `the first places by score` `the quota of positions` (filter `is in the first round` cs)

GIVEN cs IS A LIST OF `candidate for the quota of positions`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `places left after the first round` cs IS
    `the quota of positions` MINUS count (`promoted in the first round` cs)

GIVEN cs IS A LIST OF `candidate for the quota of positions`
GIVETH A LIST OF `candidate for the quota of positions`
DECIDE `promoted in the second round` cs IS
    `the first places by score` (`places left after the first round` cs)
        (filter (GIVEN c YIELD (`is in the second round` c) AND (NOT `is in the first round` c)) cs)

GIVEN cs IS A LIST OF `candidate for the quota of positions`
GIVETH A LIST OF `candidate for the quota of positions`
DECIDE `promoted in the third round` cs IS
    `the third round` (`places left after the first round` cs MINUS count (`promoted in the second round` cs))
        (filter (GIVEN c YIELD (NOT `is in the first round` c) AND (NOT `is in the second round` c)) cs)

-- Worked examples: a grade 6 teacher with the hours, three years in grade 6
-- by 1.9.2014 and a sufficient evaluation is in the first round; with 36
-- months only by 1.8.2015 and retiring, he is not in the second (the
-- decision's 37 months apply by then).
GIVEN m14 IS A NUMBER, m15 IS A NUMBER, retiring IS A BOOLEAN, score IS A NUMBER, g IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `candidate for the quota of positions`
DECIDE `a candidate with` m14 m15 retiring score g IS
    `candidate for the quota of positions` WITH
        `to grade`                                    IS g
        `professional development hours completed on` IS JUST (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2014)
        `months in the grade below on 1.9.2014`       IS m14
        `months in the grade below on 1.8.2015`       IS m15
        `months in the grade below on 31.8.2015`      IS m15
        `evaluation of תשע"ב sufficient for the grade` IS TRUE
        `retires on 31.8.2015`                        IS retiring
        `evaluation score of תשע"ה`                   IS score

#ASSERT `is in the first round` (`a candidate with` 36 47 FALSE 80 7)
#ASSERT NOT `is in the second round` (`a candidate with` 25 36 TRUE 80 7)
#ASSERT `is in the second round` (`a candidate with` 26 37 TRUE 80 7)

-- Three candidates for two places: the first round takes the one ready on
-- 1.9.2014; the third round, of the other two, the higher score.
`three candidates` MEANS
    LIST `a candidate with` 36 47 FALSE 50 7, `a candidate with` 20 40 FALSE 60 7, `a candidate with` 20 40 FALSE 90 8

#ASSERT map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `to grade`) (`the third round` 1 (filter (GIVEN c YIELD NOT `is in the first round` c) `three candidates`)) EQUALS LIST 8
#ASSERT count (`promoted in the first round` `three candidates`) EQUALS 1

-- F-ofek-hadash-maakav-2015-b's evidence: round (1)(ב) names grade 9's
-- period, rounds (2)(ב) and (3)(ב) do not, though each promotes to grade 9.
`the grades the second and third rounds' periods name` MEANS LIST 7, 8
`the grades the second and third rounds promote to` MEANS LIST 7, 8, 9
`rounds two and three ask no period for grade 9` MEANS
    (elem 9 `the grades the second and third rounds promote to`) AND (NOT elem 9 `the grades the second and third rounds' periods name`)
#ASSERT `rounds two and three ask no period for grade 9`

-- F-ofek-hadash-maakav-2015-c's evidence: 1,801 teachers who meet the
-- first round's conditions are more than the places, and the round says
-- only that they "will be promoted".
`the first round promotes every teacher who meets it, as written` MEANS TRUE
`more teachers meet the first round than there are places` MEANS
    1801 GREATER THAN `the quota of positions` AND `the first round promotes every teacher who meets it, as written`
#ASSERT `more teachers meet the first round than there are places`

§§ `ט. מה אינו נגרע מהסכם אופק חדש`

-- Nothing in §§א–ו derogates from §38(א), (ג), (ד), (ה), (ז), (ח), (י),
-- (יא) and §48. F-ofek-hadash-maakav-2015-a: §ו approves its 1,800
-- promotions "notwithstanding §38(ז)", and §ט names §38(ז) among the
-- clauses §§א–ו do not derogate from. The reading adopted (convention
-- precedence.specific): §ו's own "על אף" governs the 1,800, beyond the
-- quotas; §38(ז) stands for every other promotion.
@ref akn:art_i
`the clauses of §38 §ט keeps` MEANS
    LIST "א", "ג", "ד", "ה", "ז", "ח", "י", "יא"

`the clause of §38 §ו overrides` MEANS "ז"

`§ט keeps the clause §ו overrides` MEANS
    elem `the clause of §38 §ו overrides` `the clauses of §38 §ט keeps`
#ASSERT `§ט keeps the clause §ו overrides`

GIVEN `within the 1,800` IS A BOOLEAN, `free places in §38(ז)'s quota` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a promotion to grades 7–9 has a place` `within the 1,800` `free places in §38(ז)'s quota` IF
    `within the 1,800` OR `free places in §38(ז)'s quota` GREATER THAN 0

#ASSERT `a promotion to grades 7–9 has a place` TRUE 0
#ASSERT NOT `a promotion to grades 7–9 has a place` FALSE 0
